Distinguish a continuing effort from a particular occurrence within it. Follow-up tasks and outcomes of a bounded occurrence remain details of that occurrence; they do not by themselves establish a separate continuing effort. An ongoing effort may contain many distinct occurrences. A made object and the effort to produce or maintain it can likewise be distinct subjects when the source establishes both.
